COMET WARNING: String value length exceeds 1000 characters and will be truncated. Provided value: 'Find every adult butterfly in the image. Include only adult butterflies; exclude moths, caterpillars, pupae, other insects, shadows and flowers. Draw one tight axis-aligned bounding box per butterfly, enclosing all visible wings, body, antennae and legs. For occluded or cropped butterflies enclose only visible parts; do not invent hidden parts. Return exactly one line of valid JSON (one JSONL record), with no Markdown, code fences, explanations, confidence scores or additional keys. The record must have exactly these keys: "photo_id" (the integer ID supplied below), "boxes" (an array of boxes), and "error" (null). Each box must have exactly four numeric fields: "left", "top", "width", "height". Coordinates are normalized to the original image: left=x_min/image_width, top=y_min/image_height, width=(x_max-x_min)/image_width, height=(y_max-y_min)/image_height. The origin is the top-left corner. All numbers must be finite; left and top must be at least 0, width and height must be strictly positive, and left+width<=1 and top+height<=1. Use decimals in [0,1], never pixels or a 0-1000 scale. If there are no adult butterflies, return "boxes": []. Example structure (not the answer to this image): {"photo_id":123,"boxes":[{"left":0.1,"top":0.2,"width":0.3,"height":0.4}],"error":null}.'
COMET WARNING: String value length exceeds 1000 characters and will be truncated. Provided value: '请找出图像中所有成年蝴蝶（包括弄蝶），排除飞蛾、毛毛虫、蛹和其他昆虫。每只蝴蝶只画一个紧密的轴对齐矩形框，包含所有可见的翅膀、身体、触角和足。先在心里确定整只蝴蝶的最左、最上、最右、最下边界，再计算框的位置和大小。只输出一行合法JSON，且只有photo_id、boxes、error三个键。photo_id使用给定的整数ID，error必须为null。boxes是数组；每个框必须包含left、top、width、height四个命名数值字段。left是左边界除以整张图宽度，top是上边界除以整张图高度，width是框的总宽度除以图宽，height是框的总高度除以图高。width不是右边界，height不是下边界。所有坐标必须是0到1的小数，left>=0，top>=0，width>0，height>0，left+width<=1，top+height<=1。没有蝴蝶时boxes为[]。不要输出解释、Markdown或中间步骤。
Return exactly one line of valid JSON (one JSONL record), with no Markdown, code fences, explanations, confidence scores or additional keys. The record must have exactly these keys: "photo_id" (the integer ID supplied below), "boxes" (an array of boxes), and "error" (null). Each box must have exactly four numeric fields: "left", "top", "width", "height". Coordinates are normalized to the original image: left=x_min/image_width, top=y_min/image_height, width=(x_max-x_min)/image_width, height=(y_max-y_min)/image_height. The origin is the top-left corner. All numbers must be finite; left and top must be at least 0, width and height must be strictly positive, and left+width<=1 and top+height<=1. Use decimals in [0,1], never pixels or a 0-1000 scale. If there are no adult butterflies, return "boxes": []. Example structure (not the answer to this image): {"photo_id":123,"boxes":[{"left":0.1,"top":0.2,"width":0.3,"height":0.4}],"error":null}. The first character of your response must be { and the last character must be }. Do not wrap the JSON in triple backticks or code fences.'
